MICROSOFT ENTRA CONNECT INSTALLATION & CONFIGURATION GUIDE

PURPOSE
Microsoft Entra Connect (formerly Azure AD Connect) synchronizes on-premises Active Directory users, groups, and contacts with Microsoft Entra ID, allowing users to access Microsoft 365 and other cloud resources using their existing AD credentials.

=====================================================================
PREREQUISITES
=====================================================================

ACTIVE DIRECTORY REQUIREMENTS
- Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) installed and operational
- Forest Functional Level: Windows Server 2003 or higher
- Writable Domain Controller available
- User Principal Names (UPNs) match a verified Microsoft 365 domain

SERVER REQUIREMENTS
- Windows Server 2016, 2019, or 2022
- Domain-joined server
- Full GUI installation (Server Core not supported)
- Minimum 6 GB RAM recommended
- TLS 1.2 enabled

ACCOUNT REQUIREMENTS
- Enterprise Administrator account (Active Directory)
- Global Administrator account (Microsoft Entra ID)

=====================================================================
DOWNLOAD MICROSOFT ENTRA CONNECT
=====================================================================

1. Open:
   https://entra.microsoft.com

2. Navigate to:
   Microsoft Entra ID
     → Microsoft Entra Connect
     → Connect Sync

3. Click:
   Download the latest Entra Connect Sync Version

4. Download:
   AzureADConnect.msi

=====================================================================
INSTALLATION PROCEDURE
=====================================================================

STEP 1 - LAUNCH INSTALLER

Run:
AzureADConnect.msi

Accept the license agreement and click Continue.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 2 - CHOOSE INSTALLATION TYPE

OPTION A - EXPRESS SETTINGS (RECOMMENDED)

Use when:
- Single Active Directory Forest
- Standard synchronization deployment
- Password Hash Synchronization

OPTION B - CUSTOMIZE

Use when:
- Multiple forests
- Pass-Through Authentication
- AD FS Federation
- OU filtering requirements

---------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 3 - CONNECT TO MICROSOFT ENTRA ID

Enter:
Global Administrator credentials

Example:
admin@company.com

Click Next.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 4 - CONNECT TO ACTIVE
